From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 08:24:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: Run WPT on every ohos-main push and store the results in
 servo-ohos-wpt

Pushes to ohos-main ran no WPT, and the QuickJS WPT ran every night, also
when ohos-main had not changed, while servo-ohos-wpt built and tested
ohos-main a second time for its dashboard. The ohos-main WPT workflow runs
the whole suite with SpiderMonkey and with QuickJS on each push instead,
on the checked-release builds of the self-hosted runners. Its results job
calls store.yml of servo-ohos-wpt, which stores the results together with
those of servo/servo's CI for the upstream base, so servo-ohos-wpt no
longer runs tests itself. The QuickJS schedule goes, as the push runs
replace it.

Runs go one at a time, so that the results job, which names and pushes
the runs, never races with itself: a push waits for the running run, and
of several waiting pushes GitHub only keeps the latest.

linux-wpt.yml passes the whole `github` context to the WPT steps, which
on push events includes every pushed commit. After a rebase onto upstream
that is several hundred kilobytes (about 340 KB for the 2026-10-13 sync),
more than the 128 KiB that Linux allows for one environment variable, so
the steps could not start. Push events pass an empty context instead,
which the scripts already handle; those runs report no check run.

The results job needs the `servo-ohos-wpt` environment, limited to
ohos-main, with a SERVO_OHOS_WPT_TOKEN secret: a fine-grained token with
read and write access to the contents of openharmony-rs/servo-ohos-wpt.
It passes that secret, and no other, to store.yml, without any token
permissions.

The upstream base line needs a complete WPT run of the base in servo/servo's
merge queue, so the sync runbook checks that the merge-queue run of the new
base succeeded before tagging it.

Validation: actionlint reports nothing for ohos-main-wpt.yml and only the existing findings for quickjs.yml and linux-wpt.yml; an independent agent review found the missing secret and the context size, both checked against GitHub's documentation and the commits of past syncs; the runbook's `gh api` check prints `success` for the bases of the last two syncs, 5979b83191a and ab7e8fb1358; `./mach test-tidy` reports only the existing cargo-deny advisories of ohos-main. The store step of store.yml ran locally against a scratch copy of servo-ohos-wpt, with 20 wptreport chunks of ohos-main 8eaee63c99b and the servo/servo artifacts of its base 5979b83191a; the workflow itself runs on the next push.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written by the agent, which also ran the checks above)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 .github/workflows/linux-wpt.yml     |  7 +++--
 .github/workflows/ohos-main-wpt.yml | 46 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 .github/workflows/quickjs.yml       |  9 +++---
 docs/ohos-sync.md                   |  8 +++++
 python/servo/pr_jobs.py             |  4 +--
 5 files changed, 65 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 .github/workflows/ohos-main-wpt.yml

diff --git a/.github/workflows/linux-wpt.yml b/.github/workflows/linux-wpt.yml
index 803f8839099..7cf16c66990 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/linux-wpt.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/linux-wpt.yml
@@ -124,7 +124,9 @@ jobs:
             --filter-intermittents wpt-filtered-logs/linux/${{ matrix.chunk_id }}.json \
             ${{ inputs.wpt-args }}
         env:
-          GITHUB_CONTEXT: ${{ toJson(github) }}
+          # A push event lists every pushed commit; after a rebase that exceeds the 128 KiB that
+          # Linux allows for one environment variable, and the step cannot start.
+          GITHUB_CONTEXT: ${{ github.event_name == 'push' && '{}' || toJson(github) }}
       - name: Archive results (filtered)
         uses: actions/upload-artifact@v7
         if: ${{ always() }}
@@ -185,6 +187,7 @@ jobs:
             --tag="${{ inputs.name }}-wpt" \
             results/linux/*.json
         env:
-          GITHUB_CONTEXT: ${{ toJson(github) }}
+          # See "Run tests".
+          GITHUB_CONTEXT: ${{ github.event_name == 'push' && '{}' || toJson(github) }}
           GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
           RESULTS: ${{ toJson(needs.*.result) }}
diff --git a/.github/workflows/ohos-main-wpt.yml b/.github/workflows/ohos-main-wpt.yml
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..6a4d49a393d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.github/workflows/ohos-main-wpt.yml
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+# Runs the whole WPT suite with SpiderMonkey and with QuickJS on every ohos-main commit, and stores
+# the results in openharmony-rs/servo-ohos-wpt, which shows them with the results of the upstream
+# commit that ohos-main is based on: https://openharmony-rs.github.io/servo-ohos-wpt/
+#
+# The results job takes its token from the `servo-ohos-wpt` environment, which only ohos-main can
+# use.
+name: ohos-main WPT
+on:
+  push:
+    branches: ["ohos-main"]
+  workflow_dispatch:
+
+# One run at a time, so that the results job stores the runs in order. A push waits for the running
+# run; of several waiting pushes, GitHub only keeps the latest.
+concurrency:
+  group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}
+  cancel-in-progress: false
+
+jobs:
+  linux:
+    name: Linux
+    uses: ./.github/workflows/linux.yml
+    secrets: inherit
+    with:
+      profile: checked-release
+      wpt: true
+
+  quickjs:
+    name: QuickJS
+    uses: ./.github/workflows/quickjs.yml
+    secrets: inherit
+    with:
+      profile: checked-release
+      wpt: true
+
+  # Stores the configurations whose WPT jobs uploaded the results of all chunks, also if some
+  # tests had unexpected results.
+  results:
+    name: Results
+    needs: [linux, quickjs]
+    if: ${{ !cancelled() }}
+    uses: openharmony-rs/servo-ohos-wpt/.github/workflows/store.yml@main
+    # The called workflow reads the secret from its job's environment, but only if it is passed.
+    secrets:
+      SERVO_OHOS_WPT_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.SERVO_OHOS_WPT_TOKEN }}
+    permissions: {}
diff --git a/.github/workflows/quickjs.yml b/.github/workflows/quickjs.yml
index 286c5f7bfe8..a4fc8eb474a 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/quickjs.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/quickjs.yml
@@ -1,11 +1,10 @@
 # Builds servoshell on the QuickJS mozjs shim (openharmony-rs/servo-quickjs) and runs WPT with it,
 # against the expectations with their `js_engine == "quickjs"` conditions. Pull requests run WPT
 # on the directories of the Linux WPT job, and the whole suite when they change the shim pin
-# (python/servo/pr_jobs.py); the merge queue runs the build and smoketest only.
+# (python/servo/pr_jobs.py); the merge queue runs the build and smoketest only, and ohos-main-wpt.yml
+# the whole suite on every ohos-main push.
 name: QuickJS
 on:
-  schedule:
-    - cron: "30 1 * * *"
   workflow_call:
     inputs:
       profile:
@@ -48,7 +47,7 @@ env:
   # Replaces the servo-quickjs commit pinned in support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml, if set.
   SERVO_QUICKJS_REF: ${{ inputs.servo-quickjs-ref }}
   PROFILE: ${{ inputs.profile || 'release' }}
-  RUN_WPT: ${{ github.event_name == 'schedule' || inputs.wpt }}
+  RUN_WPT: ${{ inputs.wpt }}
 
 jobs:
   build:
@@ -139,7 +138,7 @@ jobs:
   # comments on the pull request.
   wpt:
     needs: build
-    if: ${{ github.event_name == 'schedule' || inputs.wpt }}
+    if: ${{ inputs.wpt }}
     uses: ./.github/workflows/linux-wpt.yml
     with:
       profile: ${{ inputs.profile || 'release' }}
diff --git a/docs/ohos-sync.md b/docs/ohos-sync.md
index 3cb72fa9918..94eb3566bdd 100644
--- a/docs/ohos-sync.md
+++ b/docs/ohos-sync.md
@@ -73,11 +73,19 @@ A rebase can go wrong in three ways, and each needs its own evidence:
 
 ```sh
 git fetch upstream main
+gh api "repos/servo/servo/actions/runs?head_sha=$(git rev-parse upstream/main)&event=merge_group" \
+  --jq '.workflow_runs[] | select(.name == "Main") | .conclusion'
 git tag pre-sync/<date> ohos-main
 git tag base/<date> upstream/main
 git worktree add -b ohos-sync-<date> <worktree-dir> ohos-main
 ```
 
+The base needs a complete WPT run in servo/servo's merge queue, whose results
+[servo-ohos-wpt](https://github.com/openharmony-rs/servo-ohos-wpt) shows as the
+upstream base line: the `gh api` command must print `success`, which means that
+all WPT chunks ran. Otherwise, tag the newest earlier upstream commit for which
+it does as `base/<date>` instead of `upstream/main`.
+
 Use a private cargo target dir for the worktree (see the workspace
 `AGENTS.md` if working in the servo-workspace container).
 
diff --git a/python/servo/pr_jobs.py b/python/servo/pr_jobs.py
index f09f62e911e..da52ef4f6d6 100644
--- a/python/servo/pr_jobs.py
+++ b/python/servo/pr_jobs.py
@@ -16,8 +16,8 @@ Every pull request runs the Linux unit tests and lint. On top of that:
 - WPT tests or expectations: a Linux WPT run of the directories of those tests, with SpiderMonkey
   and QuickJS, or of the whole suites for more than `MAX_DIRECTORIES` directories.
 - Files that no build or test reads, such as documentation: nothing.
-- Anything else: the OHOS and QuickJS builds and the whole Linux WPT suite. The nightly QuickJS
-  workflow runs the whole QuickJS WPT suite.
+- Anything else: the OHOS and QuickJS builds and the whole Linux WPT suite. The whole QuickJS WPT
+  suite runs on every ohos-main push (ohos-main-wpt.yml).
 
 The selections of the changed files add up, so other files that need a full run keep the QuickJS
 WPT run of changed tests or of a changed QuickJS build.
